# =============================================================================
# fragilis — Marks a test as fragile
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Marks a test as fragile — `fragilis <number>` (en `flaky`) takes a
#     non-negative integer literal.
#   • `faber test` rejects every `fragilis` case in 1.17.0: the body does not
#     run and the case is reported as failed with
#     `fragilis is rejected — flaky retries are not executed`.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Using `fragilis` to allow a test to fail or to retry it — `faber test`
#     fails the case whether its body would pass or fail. The case below fails
#     under `faber test` for that reason.
# =============================================================================

# fragilis — flaky test modifier (rejected by faber test)
#
# GRAMMAR:
#   testModifier :← 'fragilis' integer
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT:
#   No incipit — declaration or test-runner surface only.
#
# BACKEND:
#   declaration-only test modifier (whitelist: fragilis/fragilis.fab).
#

test "fragile case" flaky 1 {
    assert true
}
